codex
Implemented a self-contained Track B generator based on the paper’s Section 3 minimum-intersection positive 1-in-3 SAT problem—not the graph-root target itself. The paper confirms the problem definition, NP-completeness result, and the girth-six polynomial-time boundary. [arXiv paper](https://arxiv.org/html/1210.7684v1)

Deliverables:

- [gen_1210_7684.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1210.7684/gen_1210_7684.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1210.7684/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1210.7684/README.md)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1210.7684/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1210.7684/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1210.7684/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)
- Additional shipping-level bare diagnostic: [g9_bare_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1210.7684/g9_bare_transcript.jsonl)

All local gates pass:

- 0/200,000 structure-aware guesses
- Five attacks at 0/8 successes each
- Reference algorithm succeeds 8/8 at 12,608 operations
- 20/20 canonical-key diversity and relabeling checks
- Answer: 293 characters, 64 atoms
- Intended route: 256 operations

The only blocker is external: every hardening and G9 call returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.” Those script-owned error transcripts are preserved, but they do not establish an oracle hardness verdict. A funded/replaced `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` is required before submission.
